s"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/underestimatedCount":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"underestimatedCount","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"underestimatedCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/underestimatedCount","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/underestimatedcount","role":"symbol"}}}